(7522480, 1202162, 30364, '<td valign="top">It''s beautiful; now I''m torn between this and the blue.  So 1st place and 39th place are equally interesting for me.  I''ll give you both the same post-challenge 10 (sorry I missed voting on this challenge).</td>', 'It''s beautiful; now I''m torn between this and the blue.  So 1st place and 39th place are equally interesting for me.  I''ll give you both the same post-challenge 10 (sorry I missed voting on this challenge).', '2017-07-10 05:58:15.000000', NULL, 0),
(7522484, 1202132, 32108, '<td valign="top">very neat</td>', 'very neat', '2017-07-10 07:01:25.000000', NULL, 0),
(7522486, 1201848, 54446, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by primabarbara:</b></div><hr/><i> this is such a gorgeous shot - just not for this challenge theme apparently. What a pity! </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>I just don''t prefer to do staged, set-up shots of any kind.  There are so many subjects of interest (to me) in nature, all year long, that I avoid photography indoors of the mundane.  My experience at DPC is that any shot I take for a challenge like this is voted low.  So, I shot my creative interpretation of this challenge.  Osprey have kitchens, too!  This makes sense to me, but obviously, most voters chose to punish something so "out of the box".  The lack of tolerance at DPC by some is causing me to drift away.  I once had the philosophy to enter every challenge to expand skill set and widen horizons.  Now, the site has narrowed down and the some of the vocal and dominant personalities are being bullies.</td>', 'Originally posted by primabarbara: this is such a gorgeous shot - just not for this challenge theme apparently. What a pity!   I just don''t prefer to do staged, set-up shots of any kind.  There are so many subjects of interest (to me) in nature, all year long, that I avoid photography indoors of the mundane.  My experience at DPC is that any shot I take for a challenge like this is voted low.  So, I shot my creative interpretation of this challenge.  Osprey have kitchens, too!  This makes sense to me, but obviously, most voters chose to punish something so "out of the box".  The lack of tolerance at DPC by some is causing me to drift away.  I once had the philosophy to enter every challenge to expand skill set and widen horizons.  Now, the site has narrowed down and the some of the vocal and dominant personalities are being bullies.', '2017-07-10 08:26:55.000000', NULL, 0),
